From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tu Dinh <ngoc-tu.dinh@vates.tech>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:12:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] x86/vpt: Validate timer object with generation number
Content-Type: text/plain; charset = "utf-8"
Content-Transfert-Encoding: 8bit

The remote completion path of pt_update_irq removes timers from tm_list
by checking that their addresses match the previous iteration. However,
if the guest rearms a timer during the gap between two list iterations,
the resulting timer object is no longer the same, even if their
addresses match. Removing the timer from the list will then lose the
armed timer object.

Record a generation number in each timer object upon arming, and check
that the generation number matches before removing it from the list.

Fixes: 0bcbc971feaa ("x86/vpt: add support for level interrupts")
Signed-off-by: Tu Dinh <ngoc-tu.dinh@vates.tech>
Reviewed-by: Jan Beulich <jbeulich@suse.com>
(cherry picked from commit ad987b59ba7b434c1ebcd927328ff3cef24a193a)
Signed-off-by: Thierry Escande <thierry.escande@vates.tech>
---
 xen/arch/x86/hvm/vpt.c             | 7 ++++++-
 xen/arch/x86/include/asm/hvm/vpt.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xen/arch/x86/hvm/vpt.c b/xen/arch/x86/hvm/vpt.c
index cc8ef34f5b..2682aa87e0 100644
--- a/xen/arch/x86/hvm/vpt.c
+++ b/xen/arch/x86/hvm/vpt.c
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@ int pt_update_irq(struct vcpu *v)
 {
     struct list_head *head = &v->arch.hvm.tm_list;
     struct periodic_time *pt, *temp, *earliest_pt;
-    uint64_t max_lag;
+    uint64_t max_lag, generation;
     int irq, pt_vector = -1;
     bool level;
 
@@ -368,6 +368,7 @@ int pt_update_irq(struct vcpu *v)
     }
 
     earliest_pt->irq_issued = 1;
+    generation = earliest_pt->generation;
     irq = earliest_pt->irq;
     level = earliest_pt->level;
 
@@ -424,6 +425,9 @@ int pt_update_irq(struct vcpu *v)
         list_for_each_entry ( pt, &v->arch.hvm.tm_list, list )
             if ( pt == earliest_pt )
             {
+                if ( pt->generation != generation )
+                    break;
+
                 pt_irq_fired(v, pt);
                 cb = pt->cb;
                 cb_priv = pt->priv;
@@ -562,6 +566,7 @@ void create_periodic_time(
     set_timer(&pt->timer, pt->scheduled);
 
     pt_vcpu_lock(v);
+    pt->generation++;
     pt->on_list = 1;
     list_add(&pt->list, &v->arch.hvm.tm_list);
     pt_vcpu_unlock(v);
diff --git a/xen/arch/x86/include/asm/hvm/vpt.h b/xen/arch/x86/include/asm/hvm/vpt.h
index 74c0cedd11..7e148e7b21 100644
--- a/xen/arch/x86/include/asm/hvm/vpt.h
+++ b/xen/arch/x86/include/asm/hvm/vpt.h
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ struct periodic_time {
     u8 irq;
     struct vcpu *vcpu;          /* vcpu timer interrupt delivers to */
     u32 pending_intr_nr;        /* pending timer interrupts */
+    uint64_t generation;        /* distinguish two armings of the same timer */
     u64 period;                 /* frequency in ns */
     s_time_t scheduled;         /* scheduled timer interrupt */
     u64 last_plt_gtime;         /* platform time when last IRQ is injected */
-- 
